course: dictionary
lesson: 11649
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around it, which is the context. «The articulated lorry turned slowly at the corner.» Lorries and buses do not usually have bendy middles, so the words lorry and corner tell you articulated describes a vehicle with a joint.
explain: Articulated can also describe something with joints, like a toy figure that bends at the elbows. «The toy robot had articulated arms, so it could bend them.» Joints are the places where two parts meet and move, like your knee or elbow.
explain: Articulated is also the past form of the verb articulate, which means to say or express something clearly. «She articulated her ideas clearly in the debate.» Here the clue is ideas and debate, which are about speaking and explaining.
fact: Articulated can be an adjective, or the past form of the verb articulate.
fact: An articulated lorry or bus has two or more parts joined by a bendy joint, so it can turn corners.
fact: In the US, an articulated lorry is often called a semi-truck.
fact: An articulated skeleton has its bones joined together.
fact: «Articulate» means to say something clearly, so «she articulated her ideas» means she explained them clearly.
exercise: «The articulated bus turned the corner slowly.» What does articulated describe? | A bus that is always late | *A bus with two parts joined by a bendy joint | A bus that is painted red | A bus that is completely empty
exercise: «Her toy figure had articulated arms and legs.» What does articulated mean here? | Very loud and noisy | *Having joints that bend | Stuck firmly to the floor | Made of soft wood
exercise: «He articulated his ideas clearly in the class debate.» What does articulated mean? | Hidden away from everyone | Written in very small pencil | *Expressed clearly in words | Thrown into the bin
test: «The lorry needed lots of room to turn because it was articulated.» Why did it need so much room? | It could fly over the cars | It had no wheels at all | It was very small and light | *Its two parts bend at a joint, so it needs space to turn
test: «The museum skeleton was articulated, so all its bones were joined.» What does articulated mean here? | Having its bones painted gold | Having no bones inside it | *Having its bones joined together | Having its bones broken into pieces
exam: Mia said, «I articulated my plan to the head teacher.» What does articulated mean here? | Drew a picture of the plan | Forgot the plan completely | *Explained clearly in words | Bent the plan into a shape
